WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.304
Market research drives growth in three ways.

00:00:03.354 --> 00:00:05.827
First, identify where to play.

00:00:05.877 --> 00:00:07.761
Then execute how to win.

00:00:07.811 --> 00:00:11.650
Finally, evaluate performance with the metrics that matter.

00:00:12.367 --> 00:00:14.569
A university asks where to play.

00:00:14.619 --> 00:00:17.977
Demand data maps every course on attractiveness and performance,

00:00:18.027 --> 00:00:20.301
showing which programs to grow.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:23.674
But numbers can't say why students choose.

00:00:23.724 --> 00:00:26.150
So qualitative research guides how to win,

00:00:26.200 --> 00:00:27.000
shaping the offer,

00:00:26.601 --> 00:00:29.462
the positioning and the creative.

00:00:30.167 --> 00:00:33.572
Then track customer experience, brand and sentiment.

00:00:33.622 --> 00:00:34.740
Use it like this:

00:00:34.790 --> 00:00:35.919
for any brand,

00:00:35.969 --> 00:00:39.989
name the research at each stage and the decision it unlocks.
